invariant: INV-38
file: src/tls_write_rules.h
catches: test/zig-build-check.sh
reason: inv38-writable-len-in-place-counts-key-update's edit, with the Zig
  API as the catcher: writable_len keeps room for a KeyUpdate record that
  seal writes into side_buf, so a caller that sizes its seal by it cuts
  every write 27 bytes short. loop_record.zig and loop_key_limit.zig hold
  writable_len to each seal's own records, and fail.

--- old
    size_t records = 0;
    size_t fill = records_fill(cap, limit, &records);
    if (records > per_key) {
--- new
    size_t records = 0;
    size_t room = cap > CH_KEY_UPDATE_RECORD_LEN ? cap - CH_KEY_UPDATE_RECORD_LEN : 0;
    size_t fill = records_fill(room, limit, &records);
    if (records > per_key) {
